<title>UK: Scottish Highland shows debut premium.</title>
<headline>Scottish Highland shows debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Scottish Highland Hotels Plc showed a 10 percent premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange on Monday.</p>
<p>By 1000 GMT the shares were trading at 137-1/2p, 12-1/2p above their placing price of 125p. Volume reached 578,012 shares.</p>
<p>The issue valued the company at 30.4 million stg, raising 8.4 million stg for expansion. The chain owns six hotels in central Scotland including the Marine Hotel in Troon, which will host the Open Golf Championship next summer.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 745</p>
